                "content": "# TULARE LAKE BASIN\n\n# 11210900 LAKE KAWEAH NEAR LEMONCOVE, CA\n\n149\n\nLOCATION. Lat 36\u00b024'53\", long 119\u00b000'07\" in SE4SW4 sec.25, T.17 S., R.27 E., Tulare County, in control tower near left abutment of Terminus Dam on Kaweah River, 2.1 mi (3.4 km) northeast of Lemoncove.\n\nDRAINAGE AREA. mi 2 (1,450 km2).\n\nPERIOD OF RECORD. -October 1961 to current year. Fragmentary prior to March 1962.\n\nGAGE Water-stage recorder. Datum of gage is at mean sea level (levels by Corps of Engineers). Prior to May 22, 1962, nonrecording gage at same site and datum.\n\nREMARKS Reservoir is formed by earthfill dam and earthfill auxiliary dam, completed in February 1962. Usable 694.0 ft (211.53 m) spillway crest. Dead storage, 87 acre-ft (107,000 m\u00b3. Spillway design flood pool elevation, 745.1 ft (227.11 m), capacity, 265,994 acre-ft (328 hm\u00b3. Records, including extremes, represent capacity, 149,454 acre-ft (184 hm\u00b3) between elevations 520.0 ft (158.50 m) invert of outlet structure, and total contents at 2400 hours.",
